            "role": "assistant",
            "content": [
              {
                "type": "output_text",
                "text": "As of **today (Monday, August 3, 2026)**, here are the most relevant “latest” items tied to **Azure AI** (including Azure OpenAI / Foundry) that are showing up in official and widely reported sources:\n\n## 1) Official Azure product updates (today)\nMicrosoft’s **Azure Updates** hub is the most authoritative “what shipped” feed; it’s live-updated and filterable to **AI + Machine learning** (Azure AI Foundry, Azure OpenAI Service, etc.). ([azure.microsoft.com](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/updates/))\n\nIf you tell me which Azure AI sub-service you care about (e.g., **Azure AI Foundry**, **Azure OpenAI Service**, **Azure AI Search**, **Document Intelligence**, **Content Safety**), I can pull the newest entries specifically for that area.\n\n## 2) Recent official Azure AI announcements (late June / July 2026)\nThe Azure Blog’s **AI** tag page highlights the most recent Azure-authored posts and announcements, including:\n- “**Claude in Microsoft Foundry is now generally available**” (June 29, 2026). ([azure.microsoft.com](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/blog/tag/ai/))  \n- “**Meet Brain: The AI system behind Azure reliability**” (July 2, 2026). ([azure.microsoft.com](https://azure.microsoft.com/en-us/blog/tag/ai/))  \n\n## 3) Build 2026: agentic + Foundry-heavy Azure AI direction (still the newest “platform narrative”)\nMicrosoft’s **Build 2026** roundup page collects many of the newest platform-level launches that affect Azure AI scenarios (agents, retrieval/memory toolkits, Foundry updates, security/governance, etc.). ([news.microsoft.com](https://news.microsoft.com/build-2026/))\n\n## 4) “Today” in the broader news cycle: Microsoft AI/Azure business momentum\nSeveral “published today” articles are focused more on Microsoft’s overall AI monetization and Azure growth than on a specific Azure AI feature release—but they’re still the main “today” headlines people are circulating. ([techrepublic.com](https://www.techrepublic.com/article/news-microsoft-meta-ai-spending/))\n\n---\n\n### Quick clarification so I can give you the *right* “latest news”\nWhen you say “Azure AI,” do you mean:\n1) **New feature releases** (GA/preview changes) in Azure AI services, or  \n2) **Microsoft corporate/Azure earnings & strategy news** related to AI, or  \n3) **Azure OpenAI / Foundry model availability** updates?\n\nReply with **1 / 2 / 3** (and any service name), and I’ll summarize the newest items accordingly.",
